  "slug": "spatial-transcriptomics-expression-generation-09b0",
  "summary": "November 2025 work extends label-free self-supervised learning across spatial transcriptomics, multiplexed imaging, cardiac MR, and brain graphs.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread across these items is self-supervised representation learning, which replaces labels with structure intrinsic to the data. Two spatial transcriptomics papers, ST-GCP and MaskGraphene, use graph neural networks with contrastive or masked objectives; ST-GCP adds gene-expression permutation, and MaskGraphene jointly embeds multi-slice, multi-condition data. The imaging items extend this logic to tissue and organ scales: SSGAT identifies regions of interest in 3D tissue images, BASSL-MI finds tumor niches in CODEX imaging with reduced batch effects, and masked modeling of sparse cardiac MR planes yields a latent space for function assessment. The brain-connectome preprint applies an unsupervised graph transformer autoencoder with functional gradient geometry. What is new is attention to batch and condition structure in the data, alongside geometry-aware and masked objectives. The items do not benchmark against each other, so no relative performance claims are made.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-06"
}
